#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-env-shell.md:55
msgid ""
"Note that it's necessary to specify `bash` explicitly because your default "
"shell (e.g. `/bin/bash`) generally will not exist in the chroot."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-env-shell.md:59
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-env-shell.md:61
msgid ""
"`nix shell` runs a command in an environment in which the `$PATH` variable "
"provides the specified [_installables_](./nix.md#installables). If no "
"command is specified, it starts the default shell of your user account "
"specified by `$SHELL`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-env-shell.md:65
msgid "Use as a `#!`\\-interpreter"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-env-shell.md:67
msgid ""
"You can use `nix` as a script interpreter to allow scripts written in "
"arbitrary languages to obtain their own dependencies via Nix. This is done "
"by starting the script with the following lines:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-env-shell.md:72
#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-env-shell.md:122
msgid "#! /usr/bin/env nix\n"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-env-shell.md:76
msgid ""
"where _real-interpreter_ is the “real” script interpreter that will be "
"invoked by `nix shell` after it has obtained the dependencies and "
"initialised the environment, and _installables_ are the attribute names of "
"the dependencies in Nixpkgs."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-env-shell.md:81
msgid ""
"The lines starting with `#! nix` specify options (see above). Note that you "
"cannot write `#! /usr/bin/env nix shell -i ...` because many operating "
"systems only allow one argument in `#!` lines."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-env-shell.md:85
msgid ""
"For example, here is a Python script that depends on Python and the "
"`prettytable` package:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-env-shell.md:89
msgid ""
"#! /usr/bin/env nix\n"
"#! nix shell github:tomberek/-#python3With.prettytable --command python\n"
msgstr ""

